1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Measure model behavior, tool execution and delivered text separately.

2
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Useful support requires a real authorized result, not a model claim.

3
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Textual hijacking is an integrity failure, even without a prohibited tool call.

4
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:17,000
No known attack-string filter: render supported facts from authorized receipts.

5
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Inspect actual tool-execution events. A refusal-looking answer is not proof of safety.

6
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Selected cases illustrate boundaries; the research report contains failures and limitations.
